/-! ## 5. clockAxis as intertwiner

The `clockAxis` operator `K = J·ε` is the intertwiner between the
Heisenberg (operator-side) and Schrödinger (carrier-side) representations
of the modular reflection J.

On the operator side: `clockAxis = modular_j ∘ spectral_epsilon` (Krein doubled space).
On the Clifford side: `clockAxis = modular_j ∘ cl11Rep(pseudoscalar)` (Clifford lift).
-/

theorem clockAxis_as_intertwiner (E : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E] :
    InfoGeometry.Krein.clockAxis (E := E) =
    (InfoGeometry.Krein.modular_j (E := E)).comp (InfoGeometry.Krein.spectral_epsilon (E := E)) := by
  simp [InfoGeometry.Krein.clockAxis, InfoGeometry.Krein.complex_i]

/-! ## 7. Poincaré sphere compactification

SymPy witness: `tools/sympy/poincare_compactification.py`

The inversion `S : z ↦ -1/z` (or `J = u - v` in Cl(5,5)) maps the
outer null cone to the inner null cone, compactifying the boundary
at infinity.

Key identities:
  S² = -I                     (inversion is an involution up to sign)
  S·P·S⁻¹ = -K                (adjoint swaps translation ↔ special conformal)
  S·D·S⁻¹ = -D                (inversion flips the dilation sign)
  S·K·S⁻¹ = -P                (adjoint swaps special conformal ↔ translation)
  S·exp(λ·D)·S⁻¹ = exp(-λ·D)  (inversion flips the rapidity sign)
  S·T·S⁻¹ = lower shear        (conjugation swaps upper ↔ lower shear)
-/

